  "context": "Prioritize statistical methodology connected to Mauro Bernardi’s research: quantile and distributional regression; variational inference and scalable Bayesian computation; sparse and adaptive penalisation, variable selection and degrees of freedom; functional regression and local sparsity; statistical networks, graphical models and high-dimensional covariance or precision matrix estimation; hierarchical and generalized linear mixed models; and dynamic, state-space and time-series models. Favor contributions with clear inferential, theoretical or computational advances, including uncertainty quantification, model selection and interpretable dependence structures. Spatial statistics and applications in economics, finance, sport and the environment are relevant when they advance these methods. Give lower priority to generic deep learning, reinforcement learning and graph neural network applications without a substantial statistical contribution. Optimisation is a primary interest when connected to statistical estimation or learning: ADMM, MM algorithms, gradient and stochastic-gradient methods, proximal methods and coordinate descent, including convergence, objective scaling and numerical stability. Author matches are a modest additional signal, not a requirement for selection.",
